26q4|v|To strike; -- with off. ; To exchange (usually two things of the same kind); to swop. ; To fall or descend; to rush hastily or violently. ; To beat the air, or ply the wings, with a sweeping motion or noise; to flap.	o:2149,84,4;x6v,83,2;24q4,82,1;24c2,69,5;1o45,63,6;u7s,57,3;212c,44,9;au9,40,1;1cyl,38,8;1z47,22,5;22sm,12,2;1lkl,12,1;2h97,10,5~212c,44,9;1cyl,38,8;1o45,63,6;2h97,10,5;1z47,22,5;24c2,69,5;2149,84,4;u7s,57,3;22sm,12,2;x6v,83,2;1lkl,12,1;au9,40,1;24q4,82,1	s:26dk,27,2;x32,26,2;26d7,4,2~26d7,4,2;26dk,27,2;x32,26,2	d:ovb,33,7;2148,29,13;28oo,12,23;2oc,11,5;17nk,9,22~28oo,12,23;17nk,9,22;2148,29,13;ovb,33,7;2oc,11,5	D:6he,10,5~6he,10,5
